765	  // from earlier per-register failures so the resume can proceed. Without
766	  // a side channel, a partially-broken restore is invisible. Pin the
767	  // contract: when a CSR write fails (sticky cmderr -> PB fallback path
768	  // also clears it... but with no PB fallback for tolerant CSRs, the
769	  // tail-clear is the surviving signal), the driver records the last
770	  // observed non-zero cmderr in last_observed_cmderr() / records a
